  "metadata": {
    "author": null,
    "created_at": null,
    "description": "Pressure/tension software demonstration. Original sample geometry, compression loads, CPTs, compression advice and costs are retained. Tension loads come from the accompanying sample_project/Export RFEM.xlsx through the RFEM import. Tension resistances are FICTIONAL TEST DATA: max(1, round(0.10 * effective compression resistance)) kN, per CPT, pile size and tip level. This ratio has no geotechnical basis and must not be used for real foundation design. One base plan uses the application's cheapest valid default assignment for compression and imported tension. All 303 assigned locations satisfy both checks. 25 pre-existing unresolved locations remain open; optimization includes tension and skips unsolvable locations.",
